            "review_title": "Review at Cẩm Thị Vietnamese Cuisine",
            "review_text": "LNzg\n20 contributions\n0\nDisappointed experience\nJun 2026 • Friends\nThe service was noticeably slow and lacked attention to detail. My table was not properly prepared and there were no napkins available. The staff also took my drink order incorrectly, but there was no apology or effort to address the mistake.\n\nI had to wait an unreasonable amount of time for a bowl of rice. It seemed my order had been forgotten until I reminded the staff, and even then, there was no apology or acknowledgment.\n\nRegarding the food, the soup, meat, and egg were enjoyable. However, the egg portion was quite small, and the amount of clams in the dish was very limited. The Bánh Khọt (Vietnamese savory mini pancakes) shown on the menu was also completely different from what was actually served, at a price of 165,000 VND, it looks of poor quality.\n\nOverall, this is a Vietnamese restaurant without air conditioning, and considering both the food quality and level of service, I personally do not feel the experience was worth the visit.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten June 24, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
